WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:01.270
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.474
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:02.474 --> 00:00:04.743
- [Kelly] Look how perfectly
bright you both are!

00:00:04.743 --> 00:00:06.103
- We coordinated!
- We did.

00:00:06.103 --> 00:00:07.469
- Psychically, we knew.
- I know.

00:00:07.469 --> 00:00:09.528
- I was bringin' my Nirvana
grunge moment apparently--

00:00:09.528 --> 00:00:10.361
or something.
- No!

00:00:10.361 --> 00:00:11.194
- Yeah.
- I love this!

00:00:11.194 --> 00:00:12.318
- It's like a colorful party!

00:00:12.318 --> 00:00:13.426
Have y'all met before?

00:00:13.426 --> 00:00:14.299
- No.
- No.

00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:15.847
- This is a fever dream for me.

00:00:15.847 --> 00:00:16.680
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.706
I'm flanked by Jessica Jessica Alba guys

00:00:18.706 --> 00:00:20.141
and Kelly Clark, what is this?

00:00:20.141 --> 00:00:21.698
- I like how you say Jessica!

00:00:21.698 --> 00:00:23.562
- Jessica Alba.
- Jessica.

00:00:23.562 --> 00:00:25.270
- My 12 year-old self is--

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.103
freakin' out.
- Okay, okay.

00:00:26.103 --> 00:00:27.246
- That's okay.
(audience laughing)

00:00:27.246 --> 00:00:28.079
- I promise you we're--
- My 12 year-old self.

00:00:28.079 --> 00:00:29.317
- Not that cool.
- Is really cool.

00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:30.150
(laughing together)

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.190
- If you're cool, believe it, okay!

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.277
I'm a cool girl!

00:00:32.277 --> 00:00:33.357
- Yeah, so wait a minute.

00:00:33.357 --> 00:00:35.718
- You too, you know, she's cool.

00:00:35.718 --> 00:00:37.097
(laughing together)

00:00:37.097 --> 00:00:38.345
She's cool and I'm cool, okay.

00:00:38.345 --> 00:00:40.243
- Oh my God, I love you so much, wait.

00:00:40.243 --> 00:00:41.433
So you're from New Zealand.

00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:42.266
- I'm from New Zealand.

00:00:42.266 --> 00:00:44.437
- So how old were you when
you started in comedy there?

00:00:44.437 --> 00:00:45.527
- I was 15.

00:00:45.527 --> 00:00:46.869
- [Kelly] Oh, it's like
you were young, right?

00:00:46.869 --> 00:00:48.227
- Yeah, were all very,
quite young when we,

00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:49.775
we're all very much the same,

00:00:49.775 --> 00:00:52.674
ah, in the same, you know, area.

00:00:52.674 --> 00:00:55.994
I was 15 when I started standup comedy.

00:00:55.994 --> 00:00:57.462
- That's young!
- That is young.

00:00:57.462 --> 00:00:59.285
- And bold.
- Yeah.

00:00:59.285 --> 00:01:00.444
- Yeah, no one asked me to do it.

00:01:00.444 --> 00:01:01.277
(audience laughing)

00:01:01.277 --> 00:01:02.110
- Yeah, I know, but we're you--

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:02.943
terrified?
- Yeah!

00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:03.776
- I feel like at 15, I don't know,

00:01:03.776 --> 00:01:04.757
there's a lot happening.

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:05.590
- You know what,

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.528
I was honestly more confident
than I am as an adult.

00:01:07.528 --> 00:01:08.361
I feel like--
- Oh!

00:01:08.361 --> 00:01:09.194
- I feel like when you're a teenager

00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:12.099
you have such like passion
and enthusiasm for stuff.

00:01:12.099 --> 00:01:12.932
Like I was--
- Yeah.

00:01:12.932 --> 00:01:13.765
- Just like a nerd.

00:01:13.765 --> 00:01:14.598
I had braces.

00:01:14.598 --> 00:01:17.874
I had like, I wore sweater
vests and had big curly hair

00:01:17.874 --> 00:01:19.322
and I got the braces off.

00:01:19.322 --> 00:01:20.646
That's the only thing that has changed.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.349
(laughing together)

00:01:22.349 --> 00:01:23.182
- I love your hair.

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:24.110
- Thank you very much!
- Yes!

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:25.245
- Can you see past it?

00:01:25.245 --> 00:01:26.078
I'm so sorry, she's--

00:01:26.078 --> 00:01:27.683
- [Kelly] I don't wanna don't see past it.

00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:28.862
It's amazing.
- Yeah it's great!

00:01:28.862 --> 00:01:29.695
- I always wanted curly hair

00:01:29.695 --> 00:01:31.463
'cause my hair is like
(blows raspberry) same flat.

00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:33.109
- Oh, it's where I hide all my secrets.

00:01:33.109 --> 00:01:34.749
- Yeah, yeah, hide things in there.

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:36.333
Have you been in New Zealand before?

00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:37.166
- I have.

00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:37.999
- I love it.

00:01:37.999 --> 00:01:38.832
- Yeah.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:39.665
- When was that?

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:40.498
It's beautiful!

00:01:40.498 --> 00:01:42.573
- I did a TV show in Australia--

00:01:42.573 --> 00:01:43.915
when I was 14 and 15.
- Yeah.

00:01:43.915 --> 00:01:45.319
- So I went through New Zealand--

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:46.246
every time.
- Really!

00:01:46.246 --> 00:01:47.595
- I flew back and forth.

00:01:47.595 --> 00:01:48.428
- Cute!

00:01:48.428 --> 00:01:49.332
- And everyone thought I was Māori.

00:01:49.332 --> 00:01:50.165
- Yeah, yeah!

00:01:50.165 --> 00:01:51.792
Well, yeah, no, I'm Samoan.

00:01:51.792 --> 00:01:53.669
So like, you know, but
nobody knows what that is.

00:01:53.669 --> 00:01:55.891
I just have to say The Rock.

00:01:55.891 --> 00:01:56.724
And then--
- Right.

00:01:56.724 --> 00:01:57.557
- And then they're like--

00:01:57.557 --> 00:01:58.878
"Oh yeah, I know him!"
- I know what Samoan is.

00:01:58.878 --> 00:02:00.824
- So wait, you live in London now, right?

00:02:00.824 --> 00:02:01.657
- [Rose] I do, I do.

00:02:01.657 --> 00:02:03.157
And did you just get your first apartment?

00:02:03.157 --> 00:02:05.756
- I moved in, I'm alone.

00:02:05.756 --> 00:02:07.914
It's a bachelorette pad in--

00:02:07.914 --> 00:02:09.287
swinging London.
- But is it exciting?

00:02:09.287 --> 00:02:10.120
- It is exciting.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.330
I sing to myself a lot.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.163
- Me too.

00:02:12.163 --> 00:02:13.329
- Which is so great until I realized

00:02:13.329 --> 00:02:15.281
that everyone can hear
me in the building--

00:02:15.281 --> 00:02:16.488
like 'cause I can hear.
- Oh.

00:02:16.488 --> 00:02:17.321
- Everything above me

00:02:17.321 --> 00:02:18.233
and below--
- Oh.

00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:19.169
- I'm doing two shows a night.

00:02:19.169 --> 00:02:20.156
It's been tense.
(laughing together)

00:02:20.156 --> 00:02:22.966
But it's, it's yeah, it's very fun.

00:02:22.966 --> 00:02:23.799
I do miss it though.

00:02:23.799 --> 00:02:26.261
'Cause I, so that clip
is with my real life

00:02:26.261 --> 00:02:27.989
best friend, Emma.
- I love that!

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:29.038
- Who I love that cast in the show.

00:02:29.038 --> 00:02:31.684
- Yeah, because I just can do what I like.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.517
(laughing together)

00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:34.645
and I wanted to hang
out with my best friend.

00:02:34.645 --> 00:02:36.235
And we used to live with each other--

00:02:36.235 --> 00:02:37.099
and we've moved apart.
- Yeah.

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:37.932
We broke up.
- Yeah.

00:02:37.932 --> 00:02:38.880
- Which is really sad.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.293
And the thing I miss the most

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.713
is it's so hard being hungover alone.

00:02:43.713 --> 00:02:44.546
(laughing together)

00:02:44.546 --> 00:02:45.379
You know what I mean?

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:46.935
Like you want, you want a flatmate.

00:02:46.935 --> 00:02:49.131
- You need somebody to order
a burger and a Coke with you.

00:02:49.131 --> 00:02:49.964
- Yeah, you need someone

00:02:49.964 --> 00:02:52.161
to watch like terrible television with.

00:02:52.161 --> 00:02:53.157
That is the thing I miss the most

00:02:53.157 --> 00:02:54.645
about living with someone else.

00:02:54.645 --> 00:02:55.478
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:55.478 --> 00:02:56.930
- Now I just have to
call her and be hungover,

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:57.763
over the phone--

00:02:57.763 --> 00:02:58.596
and it's not fun.
- It's not the same.

00:02:58.596 --> 00:02:59.429
- Yeah.

00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:00.441
- It's not as cool over Zoom.

00:03:00.441 --> 00:03:01.340
- Yeah, exactly.
(laughing together)

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.567
Yeah, yeah, no one wants to
accept that Zoom request.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:04.774
I don't know.
(laughing together)

00:03:04.774 --> 00:03:05.701
- Tell us about your show.

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:06.771
It looks hysterical.

00:03:06.771 --> 00:03:08.518
- Well the good thing
is I'm not a great actor

00:03:08.518 --> 00:03:10.065
so I'm very much like I am in the show.

00:03:10.065 --> 00:03:10.898
(laughing together)

00:03:10.898 --> 00:03:13.170
And so I play a character

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.521
in the show called Jessie.

00:03:14.521 --> 00:03:15.601
She's in her late twenties.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.401
She's a New Zealander living in London.

00:03:17.401 --> 00:03:18.913
What a transformative role.

00:03:18.913 --> 00:03:19.746
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:03:19.746 --> 00:03:22.162
(laughing together)

00:03:22.162 --> 00:03:24.256
- And basically in the first series

00:03:24.256 --> 00:03:28.370
on NZ, she has I'd say
an interesting encounter,

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.686
a wonderful evening with a gentleman.

00:03:30.686 --> 00:03:31.519
- Yes.
- That's the daytime.

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:32.352
- Way of saying it.

00:03:32.352 --> 00:03:33.840
(laughing together)

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.676
- An encounter, she had relations.

00:03:35.676 --> 00:03:37.567
- A brief encounter with a guy

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:40.870
who turns out to be a
very famous movie star.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.011
A kind of romcom will
they, won't, they ensues

00:03:43.011 --> 00:03:44.129
in the first series.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:44.962
And in the second series--

00:03:44.962 --> 00:03:45.813
- I love this.
- Which is out.

00:03:45.813 --> 00:03:48.169
- Yeah, it's very much,
it's a full-on romcom.

00:03:48.169 --> 00:03:49.002
- [Kelly] Love!

00:03:49.002 --> 00:03:50.617
- Which you know, I love and--
- Me too.

00:03:50.617 --> 00:03:54.064
- The second series kind
of kicks off the moment

00:03:54.064 --> 00:03:56.350
after the very ending of
the first series where she's

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.945
on a bus and she's figuring out whether

00:03:57.945 --> 00:04:00.724
or not to stay in London
or go back to New Zealand.

00:04:00.724 --> 00:04:01.557
- I like it!

00:04:01.557 --> 00:04:02.668
- Makes a very impulsive decision.

00:04:02.668 --> 00:04:03.633
And then the next series

00:04:03.633 --> 00:04:05.818
is a six-episode long anxiety attack.

00:04:05.818 --> 00:04:06.651
(laughing together)

00:04:06.651 --> 00:04:09.003
So you gotta watch it, yeah.

00:04:09.003 --> 00:04:09.836
- And it's no where.
- And it's full of regrets.

00:04:09.836 --> 00:04:11.432
- Near real life.
- Full of regrets, yeah.

00:04:11.432 --> 00:04:12.348
- Totally, yeah.

00:04:12.348 --> 00:04:14.220
- So wait, so you were about
to shoot the first show

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.434
when the pandemic hit, right?

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.267
- [Rose] Yes.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.100
- [Kelly] That stinks.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.152
- Yeah, and I went back
home to New Zealand,

00:04:20.152 --> 00:04:21.042
for like five months,

00:04:21.042 --> 00:04:21.875
because everything got--

00:04:21.875 --> 00:04:23.284
shut down.
- Wow.

00:04:23.284 --> 00:04:24.117
- I went back.

00:04:24.117 --> 00:04:24.950
- I went back, I was like, cool,

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.223
well I'm gonna have to retrain

00:04:26.223 --> 00:04:27.230
to be a farmer now.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:30.185
So the world's over and
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:30.185 --> 00:04:32.441
I truthfully didn't think
it would ever happen.

00:04:32.441 --> 00:04:34.222
I really kind of mourned the show.

00:04:34.222 --> 00:04:35.055
Like I was like, oh--

00:04:35.055 --> 00:04:36.103
- I was gonna say, did you think, yeah,

00:04:36.103 --> 00:04:37.704
it wasn't gonna happen
because of the timing?

00:04:37.704 --> 00:04:38.537
- Completely, yeah.

00:04:38.537 --> 00:04:40.836
And we came back and we
made it really safely

00:04:40.836 --> 00:04:42.419
in October of 2020.

00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:45.850
And yeah, I was shocked.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:46.683
It was a very strange--
- Yeah.

00:04:46.683 --> 00:04:48.037
- Experience though,
because there were scenes

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:49.430
in like clubs and stuff

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.764
and it was the heart of lockdown

00:04:50.764 --> 00:04:52.701
and it was like a fake club--

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:53.534
- That was hard.

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.046
- All the ESAs and like extras

00:04:55.046 --> 00:04:56.920
were really stoked secretly to be there.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.677
Like they were like, yeah, we're clubbing.

00:04:58.677 --> 00:04:59.820
This is hot!

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.653
But yeah--

00:05:00.653 --> 00:05:01.620
- We're around humans!
- They got to like it.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.453
- Exactly.
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:02.453 --> 00:05:03.286
It was very intoxicating.

00:05:03.286 --> 00:05:04.119
- I love that, I love that.

00:05:04.119 --> 00:05:05.773
Well, we have to do some commercials,

00:05:05.773 --> 00:05:08.662
but you can see Rose's
show, Starstruck, streaming

00:05:08.662 --> 00:05:09.579
on HBO Max.

